## Limits

State only what the module note supports. Candidates: one prior scale
sigma_mu^2 for both level and slopes, where Prado, Moral and Parnell
give the slopes their own prior, with no argument for the common
scale's calibration under min-max scaling; nothing on identifiability
of beta in a small or thin cell, or on the interaction between the slope
prior and lambda_c; no weighted update under soft membership, and the
variance ensemble keeps the constant basis; no approximation or
contraction result for piecewise-linear Voronoi ensembles.

## References

Chipman, H. A., George, E. I. and McCulloch, R. E. (2010). BART:
Bayesian additive regression trees. *The Annals of Applied Statistics*
4(1), 266-298. doi:10.1214/09-AOAS285

Prado, E. B., Moral, R. A. and Parnell, A. C. (2021). Bayesian additive
regression trees with model trees. *Statistics and Computing* 31, 20.
doi:10.1007/s11222-021-09997-3

Stone, A. and Gosling, J. P. (2025). AddiVortes: (Bayesian) additive
Voronoi tessellations. *Journal of Computational and Graphical
Statistics* 34(3), 859-871. doi:10.1080/10618600.2024.2414104
